  "_comment": "Soulidity 2-sig fast-path acceptance matrix (11 rows). The harness scripts/smoke-soulidity.ts is a PTB replayer: each step's transactionBase64 must be a real, pre-built PTB encoded as base64. The operator builds these PTBs ahead of time using the SDK builders in web/lib/soulidity/tx/ (e.g. via a one-off Node script that wires builders + smoke wallet keypairs against the testnet/mainnet package id from the deployment manifest), then drops the base64 strings into the placeholders below. The {{txDigest}} token in mirror bodies is substituted at runtime with the digest of the just-signed step. Mirror paths must reference live first-party routes under web/app/api (collection PTB1 mirrors hit /api/collections/create which accepts { txDigest, floorPriceAtomic? }; supply floorPriceAtomic when the collection enforces an off-chain floor). Mirror auth is picked per step.signer: publisher rows use SMOKE_PUBLISHER_*, buyer rows use SMOKE_BUYER_*, agent rows use SMOKE_AGENT_* (see .env.soulidity-smoke.example). Replace every __PLACEHOLDER__ before running. /api/souls/publish/batch syncBodies entries must be one-per-soul (length === expectedSoulCount); the operator fills each __SOUL_ON_CHAIN_ID_N__ with the actual minted soul id from the same PTB. The batch route ALWAYS requires a per-soul `sealSidecar` (Soul content is uploaded encrypted by web/lib/hooks/use-collection-publish.ts) and ALWAYS requires `memorySealSidecar` for souls that emit a founding-memory event (memory blob is also uploaded encrypted) — replace the __REPLACE_WITH_*_SEAL_SIDECAR_N__ placeholders with the real Seal envelope sidecars (shape: SealEnvelopeSidecar from web/lib/services/seal-crypto.ts) produced by the Walrus upload pipeline; the route returns 422 if either is missing. Add `assetsSealSidecar` separately on entries whose initial asset version is private (route also returns 422 then). Add `skillsSealSidecar` separately on entries whose initial skill version is private (skills uploaded with `skillsVisibility: 'private'` by use-collection-publish.ts emit a private SkillVersionAppended event and the route returns 422 if the per-soul `skillsSealSidecar` is missing). The single-Soul /api/souls/publish route enforces the same fail-closed contract: every body ALWAYS requires `sealSidecar` (the create flow at web/app/create/gas/page.tsx uploads the Soul character file as encrypted), ALWAYS requires `memorySealSidecar` when the PTB emits a founding-memory event, and ALWAYS requires `skillsSealSidecar` when the PTB appends a private initial skill version — replace the __REPLACE_WITH_SOUL_SEAL_SIDECAR__ / __REPLACE_WITH_MEMORY_SEAL_SIDECAR__ / __REPLACE_WITH_SKILLS_SEAL_SIDECAR__ placeholders below with the real envelopes. Plan source: docs/plans/2026-05-03-soulidity-2sigs-fast-path.md sections 7a/7b.",
